 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The day before: separate the eggs and slip each <b>yolk</b> into a small dish, whole.</li><li>Pour the <b>soy sauce</b> and <b>mirin</b> over, so the yolks are just covered. Cover and refrigerate <b>24 hours</b>. They turn deep amber and firm up like soft jam.</li><li>Use eggs sold for eating raw, or pasteurised ones. Keep the cured yolks cold and use them within two days.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
